 \section{Discussion, limitations, and falsifiability}
 The screen is conditional on supplied scalar prices, a supplied nonnegative quantity, and commensurate units. It does not select a social cost of carbon, estimate exergy destruction, model price endogeneity, discounting, capital turnover, uncertainty distributions, interactions, leakage, rebound, or distributional effects. Negative $q$ reverses the lower-price ordering; project-specific price pairs do not share the simple portfolio factorization. No dataset is analyzed. A real-number counterexample to an identity or a mismatch in exact-rational replay would falsify the mathematical package.
